From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael moore <mrmoore27@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:18:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/27] prime: move the rnd/a2 sketch to the note's LZT1
 attestation; weight the bonus by independence

The 100-byte on-chain signature does not fit RDTS: Knots 29.4.2 refuses a
coinbase OP_RETURN over 83 bytes (bad-txns-vout-script-toolarge; XBT-051
regtest). The commitment is now the research note's 70-byte
OP_RETURN PUSH68 "LZT1" | BLAKE2b(A) | G, with A (branches_hash,
mempool_digest, node_tag, t_gbt, plus a payout_digest so a pool cannot
lift A onto its own payout) and its signature carried off chain.

tides::sovereignty weights authored work by the entropy detector's
independence score and can cap any one gateway key's share of the pot;
the excess goes back to the pool.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
