+//! **Credit.** This is the note's "×(1+β) multiplier funded by the stratum fee", written as a
+//! pot so it can never spend more than the fee: β for a block is `pot ÷ authored work's value`.
+//! Each identity's authored work is weighted by its gateway's **independence score** (0–1, from
+//! the template-entropy detector: a gateway that tracks the pool's own template scores ~0), the
+//! pot is shared pro rata by weighted work, and each share joins the identity's carry the way
+//! rebate credits do (reversed on orphan by the same `carry_delta`). Linear pro rata is
+//! deliberate: splitting one operator into many identities or gateway keys changes nothing (up
+//! to rounding), so there is nothing to gain from Sybils. An optional **cap per gateway key**
+//! (the note's answer to one `G` shared across farms) limits any one `G` to a share of the pot;
+//! what the cap cuts goes back to the pool, not to the others, so nobody gains by pushing a rival
